Patch 2053: a draw whose vertex constants are unchanged since the previous draw of the batch shares that draw's
vertex-constant slot (VCB_SHARE=0 off).

Every draw copied all 512 vertex constants (8 KB) into its own slot of the upload heap: about 3,300 draws a J-Stars
fight frame, ~27 MB per frame of write-combined writes, mostly the same values reloaded. rsx_state's
vertex_constants_dirty (set by every constant write) now says whether anything changed since the last copy; with the
same program (the garbage-projection fallback depends on it), viewport z and batch/parity, the record points its
vcb_slot at the earlier slot. Draw records got vcb_slot; the fragment-side slot (cb_slot) is unchanged.

Tested (US disc, bench.ps1): drain per frame 18.2-19.3 ms in the demo (before 20.5) and 15.6 in the fight (before
19.3); Free Battle 23.09 flips/s (before 21.77); demo 21.96 / 21.44 / 21.20 (median 21.44, before 21.62: the demo's
frames now wait on the 60 Hz beat instead); pictures right (bench\exp\2026-11-07_2021-vcbshare).

